// chit_chat.proto
//
// gRPC API definition for the Chit Chat distributed chat service.
//
// Design choice: the Join RPC uses SERVER-SIDE streaming. A participant
// calls Join once and receives a long-lived stream over which the server
// pushes every broadcast (join/leave notifications and chat messages)
// tagged with a Lamport logical timestamp. Publishing and leaving are
// plain unary RPCs. This matches the system's topology: the service
// process is the single fan-out point, and each client only ever needs
// to receive broadcasts, never to send a stream.

